  "worked_solution": "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222d}_{R}\\frac{{e}^{z+y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20613}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{e}^{z+y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[1,e]\\times [0,\\operatorname{ln}\u20613]\\times [0,\\operatorname{ln}\u20612]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20613}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{e}^{z+y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20613}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{e}^{z}\\cdot {e}^{y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20613}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20613}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z & ={[\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x]}_{1}^{e}\\cdot {[{e}^{y}]}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20613}\\cdot {[{e}^{z}]}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (3-1)\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
